{# VARLENYX breadcrumb — MBO §7 locked rule: every interior page shows
   VARLENYX > Section > Subsection, so users always know where they are.
   Skipped entirely on the homepage (page.url == "/").
   Auto-derives the "Section" crumb by matching page.url against site.nav,
   and adds a final non-linked "Subsection" crumb from the page's own
   `title` when the page is deeper than its section landing page.
   Pages needing a fully custom trail (e.g. a specific subsection label
   that differs from `title`) can pass frontmatter:
     breadcrumb:
       - { label: "Science & Technology", url: "/science-technology/" }
       - { label: "Medicine & Clinical Innovation" }
   which overrides the auto-derivation entirely. #}
{% if page.url != "/" %}
{% set trail = page.url | breadcrumbTrail(site.nav, breadcrumb, title) %}
<nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <div class="container">
    <ol>
      {% for crumb in trail %}
      <li>
        {% if not crumb.url or loop.last %}
        <span aria-current="page">{{ crumb.label }}</span>
        {% else %}
        <a href="{{ crumb.url }}">{{ crumb.label }}</a>
        {% endif %}
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
</nav>
{% endif %}
